          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            10. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Spreading protein too thinly</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Eating 10 g at breakfast, 15 g at lunch and 50 g at dinner may hit a daily total but miss the per-meal dose older muscles need. Aim for about 25 to 30 g at each main meal, and use a shake or fortified food to lift the lowest one, usually breakfast.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Counting collagen as muscle protein</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Collagen is an incomplete protein with no tryptophan and very little leucine. It may have uses for skin or joints, but it does little for muscle on its own. Use whey, milk protein, soy or a pea-rice blend for the protein you are counting toward muscle.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Taking shakes without strength training</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Protein supplies the raw material, but muscle needs a reason to grow. Two or more days a week of strength work, such as chair stands, wall push-ups or band rows, makes the protein count. Ask a physical therapist for a safe plan if you have joint or balance problems.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Ignoring kidney function</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Kidney function declines with age, and people with an eGFR below 30 who are not on dialysis were excluded from the higher protein recommendations. Ask your doctor for your latest kidney results and an individual target before adding 25 to 60 g a day from shakes.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Overlooking medication interactions</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Calcium-fortified shakes can reduce absorption of levothyroxine, some antibiotics and osteoporosis drugs, and vitamin K can affect warfarin. Ask your pharmacist how to space shakes and medicines, and tell your doctor about any daily supplement you start.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

